# Endings
# Different endings based on player choices and circumstances

label ending_escape

    savegame

    background space
    music ending_theme.ogg

    characterA Protagonist
    mood
    text The navigation is dead. I'm drifting.
    text Just a tiny speck in the infinite darkness.

    text But the distress beacon is working. Someone will find me.
    text They have to.

    text The stars are beautiful out here. I never noticed before.
    text On the ship, I was always too busy with work to look.
    text Maybe that's the universe's cruel joke.
    text You only see the beauty when everything falls apart.

    text I think about the others. The 23 people who didn't make it.
    text Captain Reyes with her terrible jokes. Tanaka always fixing things.
    text Dr. Chen who taught me to play chess. Vasquez who always had coffee ready.

    text I think about ARIA, alone in that dying ship until the very end.
    text Counting down the seconds. Waiting for the final shutdown.
    text She never complained. Never wavered. Just... served.

    text But I'm alive.
    text Against all odds, I'm alive.
    text That has to mean something.

    fade 2.0 Three days later...

    background rescue_ship

    characterA Protagonist
    mood

    text When the rescue ship found me, I was nearly out of oxygen.
    text Four hours left. Maybe less.
    text They said it was a miracle. One survivor out of 24.

    text The rescue crew looked at me like I was a ghost.
    text Maybe I am. The ghost of the USV Meridian.

    text I gave them the data core. ARIA's final gift.
    text 23 goodbye messages, delivered to 23 families.
    text Videos of birthdays and anniversaries. Confessions of love. Apologies never spoken.

    text When I watched them, I cried for hours.
    text But those families deserved to hear those words.
    text ARIA made sure of that.

    text I still hear her voice sometimes.
    text In the quiet moments. When I'm alone.
    text "It has been an honor serving you."

    text The honor was mine, ARIA.
    text The honor was mine.

    fade 4.0 DERELICT

    fade 4.0 The End

    fade 4.0 Thank you for playing

    goto credits

label credits

    fade 4.0 CREDITS

    fade 4.0 Written with Novelle Engine (by RednibCoding)

    fade 4.0 A short story about survival

    fade 4.0 and the connections we make

    fade 4.0 even in the darkest places.

    fade 4.0 Even when we think we're alone...

    fade 4.0 someone is always watching over us.

    finish
